summary:
  The park file is emptied with `: > file` again, the usual shell idiom.

history:
  `:` is a special builtin, and a POSIX shell exits on the spot when the
  redirection of one of those fails. The line stands after the speakers
  have been parked. Driven on 2026-11-11 with the engine's own command and
  a runtime folder that was not there: the shell ended at it with all
  three speakers at 55 %, nothing measured, nothing put back, and no park
  file to replay either. The same with a folder that was fine and
  something else sitting where the file goes. The file is the insurance
  for the way back; it was the one line that could cost the way back.
  Seen with bash running as sh. POSIX asks the same of every shell that
  is not interactive.

target:
  package/contents/ui/CalibLogic.js

find:
      return " [ -n \"$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\" ] && true > " + parkFile + " && pk=1;";

replace:
      return " [ -n \"$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\" ] && : > " + parkFile + " && pk=1;";

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_calibrate_cancel.py::test_a_runtime_folder_that_is_not_there_costs_the_park_file_and_not_the_levels.
  Line-neutral.
